codex
The alignment refusal provides another useful observable: it prints the live `d->dmaaddr` value. After proving a successful DMA from fresh response bytes, the detector can compare readback against that independently printed value. This avoids making a hard-coded advanced cursor the read oracle.

The disabled row can then retain that same prior cursor, with enable cleared, to test the entry-value behavior and the enable-before-alignment ordering.
